// approval_gate.air — a draft, a human-approval PAUSE barrier, and the
// RESUME that continues past it (ASK + PAUSE + RESUME).
//
//  regeneration: the original  fixture (a single bare
// `ais.resume "<checkpoint-id>"`) predates the current op-spec-driven
// emitter. In the current op-spec, PAUSE and RESUME both ignore their
// attributes for text purposes (checkpoint id / message / timeout are
// runtime-only metadata, not rendered into AIR) — only their
// Data-dependency operands render, as a `[...]` bracket. Regenerated from
// Python's `GraphRecorder.to_graph().to_air()` reference emitter.
//
//   apxm validate approval_gate.air
module {
  func.func @approval_gate() -> !ais.token attributes {ais.entry} {
    %draft_change = ais.ask "Propose a change to review." : !ais.token
    %await_approval = ais.pause [%draft_change : !ais.token] : !ais.token
    %resumed = ais.resume [%await_approval : !ais.token] : !ais.token
    func.return %resumed : !ais.token
  }
}
